<title>UK: Tilbury plunge on Holzmann placement.</title>
<headline>Tilbury plunge on Holzmann placement.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Tilbury Douglas Plc plunged after its main shareholder, German construction group Philip Holzmann, announced it wanted to sell 9.9 million shares of the British building company.</p>
<p>By 1140 GMT Tilbury Douglas were down 102-1/2p to 640p in volume of 9.8 million shares.</p>
<p>&quot;There is virtually nobody wanting to touch it at higher levels&quot;, a trader said.</p>
<p>Earlier, Tilbury said investment banks UBS and Cazenove &amp; Co would place 9.9 million shares of Tilbury.</p>
<p>Holzmann announced on June 6 it would sell its 29.46 percent stake in Tilbury.</p>
<p>&quot;That has put a lot of pressure on the stock&quot;, another trader said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
